{
  "_comment": "The programs the controller's image takes from their vendors' GitHub releases as it is built, noVNC's source at its release's tag, and mkosi's, which the OS image's build runs (.github/workflows/os-image.yml, at the version image/build.sh names), each with its pin: the version, and the sha256 of the exact file for every architecture the image takes it for. The one copy: the Dockerfile and the bare-metal installer fetch each through scripts/lib/pin-fetch, which keeps a file only when it is those bytes, so an image built again holds the same files until a pin moves, and tools/pins.py --file moves it (check, move, pin, verify). A row's source is written as a toolchain's is: tarball for an archive the build unpacks, script for a file that is itself the program.",
